    "title": "Arsenal vs Man City LIVE: Carabao Cup final result, latest updates and fan reaction",
    "text": "Celebration: Manchester City lift the Carabao Cup after beating Arsenal at WembleyGetty ImagesManchester City have beaten Arsenal 2-0 in the 2025/26 Carabao Cup final at Wembley. Nico O’Reilly scored two goals in quick succession in the second half to decide Sunday’s showpiece fixture between the Premier League title rivals. Kepa Arrizabalaga made a big error for the first of those, leading to inevitable major scrutiny on Mikel Arteta’s gamble to start him over usual No1 David Raya.Arsenal’s dreams of an unprecedented trophy quadruple this season are now over, with a new injury concern over Eberechi Eze to make matters worse. City will hope to have dealt them a sizable psychological blow for the top-flight run-in, with Arteta’s side - who have a nine-point advantage at the summit with seven games to go, having played a match more - still having to visit the Etihad Stadium on April 19.Arsenal have two weeks now to stew on their surprising Wembley no-show during the campaign’s final international break, after which they face Southampton and Sporting in the quarter-finals of the FA Cup and Champions League respectively. City, meanwhile, host Liverpool next in a blockbuster FA Cup showdown as they celebrate winning the League Cup for the ninth time - a record fifth under the management of Pep Guardiola. Follow Arsenal vs Man City reaction live below!Arsenal vs Man City highlightsMan City lift League Cup trophy for ninth timeManchester City lift the League Cup for the ninth time overall and first since their fourth in a row in 2021.They are now only one behind record-holders Liverpool.City’s fifth under Pep Guardiola - no manager has won it more in history.Arsenal remains trophyless since the 2020 FA Cup final.They haven’t won the League Cup since 1993.They have to reset and put this disappointment behind them very quickly.The Gunners still have that nine-point lead in the title race with seven games to go - City have a game in hand and still have to play Arsenal at the Etihad on April 19 - and have very winnable quarter-final ties in both the FA Cup and Champions League, against Southampton and Sporting respectively, coming up quickly after the international break.Ben Whitley/PA WireGetty ImagesREUTERSContrasting emotions at WembleyArsenal’s players looked as crestfallen as you might expect as they went up to collect their second-place medals, led by Saka and Arteta.O’Reilly and Trafford were beaming in their post-match interviews on the pitch, meanwhile.What a day for O’Reilly. And an academy graduate to boot.An afternoon he will never forget at Wembley.John Walton/PA WireREUTERSAdam Davy/PA WireArsenal 0-2 Man CityStandard Sport’s Matt Verri at Wembley StadiumThat's an awful afternoon for Arsenal.Didn't really lay a glove on City and deservedly beaten.The trophy wait goes on and they now have two weeks to reflect on a huge disappointment.City, on the other hand, have just had rocket fuel pumped into them heading into the final weeks of the season.Arsenal 0-2 Man CityManchester City win the Carabao Cup thanks to a quick-fire second-half brace from Nico O’Reilly at Wembley.Fully deserved - Arsenal were not at the races at all in that second half.Plenty of scrutiny to follow on Mikel Arteta’s decision to pick Kepa Arrizabalaga over David Raya in goal.How big an impact will that result have in the Premier League title run-in?These rivals meet again at the Etihad Stadium in the top-flight on April 19.Arsenal’s quadruple dream is over.REUTERSArsenal 0-2 Man City94 mins: Almost over at Wembley.City’s name is being engraved onto the trophy.Arsenal 0-2 Man City93 mins: Plenty of empty seats now at the Arsenal end of Wembley as Madueke’s inviting cross to the back post is headed clear.Madueke then tries to tee up Saka from the byline, but Rodri is there to clean up for City once more.Arsenal 0-2 Man City90 mins: Four minutes of added time at Wembley.Kepa comes rushing out of his box again to boot clear under pressure from Haaland.Arsenal 0-2 Man City90 mins: Silva’s cross is held by Kepa as City break with numbers.Now they counter again and Doku whips a low shot just wide of the near post.Replays show that earlier Jesus header actually bounced off the crossbar, rather than being clawed out by Trafford.Twice Arsenal have hit the woodwork late on at Wembley.Arsenal 0-2 Man City88 mins: Arsenal are now finally throwing the kitchen sink at this as Trafford claws away at the last and Gyokeres goes down wanting a penalty.Saka also has an effort blocked.Arsenal 0-2 Man City86 mins: Finally a bit of late momentum for Arsenal as Jesus comes forward and tries to find Saka, but his pass is intercepted by Rodri - who then promptly gives it away.Arsenal have a throw-in on the far side, but it’s cleared.",
